ERROR HANDLING 2026-05-12 (cascade from PKIX-jy95.4): bridge exposes structured BridgeError + PerCertError with rich discrimination; no baked-in degradation policy.

BridgeError variants (Clone + Debug + PartialEq + Eq + Send + Sync + non_exhaustive; serde feature-gated):
- BinaryNotFound { path }
- BinaryNotExecutable { path, detail }
- SubprocessFailed { exit_code, stderr }
- SubprocessKilled { signal }
- SubprocessTimeout { elapsed_secs }
- OutputParseError { detail }

PerCertError variants:
- MalformedDer { detail }
- UnsupportedCertType { detail }
- Other { detail }

run_on_certs returns: Result<Vec<Result<Vec<(CheckId, Verdict)>, PerCertError>>, BridgeError>. Bridge-level errors fail the whole call; per-cert errors are inline entries.

ZlintBridge::new() is fallible (returns Result). BridgeConfig accepts timeout (default 60s; configurable). Version-mismatch is not checked (runtime enumeration; output-format issues surface as OutputParseError).

IMPLEMENTATION DETAILS DEFERRED:
- Subprocess timeout impl (tokio::time::timeout vs std::process::Command + watchdog thread)
- Exact PerCertError discrimination (need to see what zlint emits)
- stderr capture vs streaming (probably full capture for diagnostics)
- Whether to expose stderr in success-path BridgeOutput for logging
